<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Age of Enlightenment</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Enlightenment</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Age of Enlightenment was an intellectual movement of the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries that emphasised reason, science, individual rights and reform of government. It shaped political thought across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and beyond. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, Enlightenment ideas influenced reformers and culminated in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-3-may-1791">Constitution of 3 May 1791</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment.jpg" alt="Age of Enlightenment" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anicet Charles Gabriel Lemonnier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Les_salons_au_XVIIIe_si%C3%A8cle_-_Histoire_Image.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In the eighteenth century the city was a centre of the German-language <b>Enlightenment</b>, home of the critics Johann Jakob Bodmer and Johann Jakob Breitinger, the poet Salomon Gessner and the writer Johann Caspar Lavater, and birthplace of the educator Johann Heinrich Pestalozzi.</blockquote><a href="/empire/canton-of-zurich">Canton of Zürich · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>His son Peter Leopold (r. 1765–1790) was one of the most consistent reformers of the <b>Enlightenment</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/grand-duchy-of-tuscany">Grand Duchy of Tuscany · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Enlightenment</b> of Montesquieu, Voltaire, Rousseau and Diderot's Encyclopédie was largely conducted in French.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-france">Kingdom of France · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>A black Jewish community on the coast, without links to Jews elsewhere, drew the interest of <b>Enlightenment</b> race scientists and of the German Loango Expedition of 1873–76.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-loango">Kingdom of Loango · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>…was for five centuries the largest state in Italy, ruled from one of Europe's greatest cities by Angevins, Aragonese, Spanish viceroys and Bourbons; a centre of humanism, Baroque culture and the <b>Enlightenment</b>, it also left the feudal and fiscal legacy that shaped the later history of southern Italy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-naples">Kingdom of Naples · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>…Polish Brethren, joined by the Italian exile Fausto Sozzini, developed at Raków a rationalist theology that influenced later <b>Enlightenment</b> thought, while the dense network of Jewish communities in Polish and Lithuanian towns formed the demographic and cultural heartland of Ashkenazi Jewry, whose Talmudic academies, Hasidic movement and Yiddish…</blockquote><a href="/empire/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
